+## Cancellation with an `AbortSignal`
+
+Pass a `signal` to reject queued tasks from the same abort source you already use for the work itself. Tasks that are already running keep going, so give them the signal too if they should stop early:
+
+```js
+import pLimit from 'p-limit';
+
+const controller = new AbortController();
+
+const limit = pLimit({concurrency: 5, signal: controller.signal});
+
+const urls = getUrls(); // Assume this returns a large list of URLs
+
+// Give up on the whole batch after 10 seconds
+setTimeout(() => {
+	controller.abort();
+}, 10_000);
+
+const results = await Promise.allSettled(
+	urls.map(url => limit(() => fetch(url, {signal: controller.signal})))
+);
+```
+
+Unlike `clearQueue()`, this also rejects tasks added after the abort, so late arrivals cannot restart the work.
+
